Mindfulness-Based Cognitive Therapy (MBCT) reduces relapse rates for recurrent depression by 43% compared to usual care — as effective as antidepressants for this indication.
A 2014 meta-analysis in JAMA Internal Medicine of 47 trials found mindfulness meditation programmes significantly improved anxiety, depression, and pain.
Mindfulness training in schools reduces anxiety symptoms in adolescents by 0.4 standard deviations — a clinically meaningful effect size comparable to small-group therapy.
